WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:01.280
So what is a date?

00:01.280 --> 00:08.400
If you take a look at the calendar and you pick any date, for example August 20th, 2025.

00:08.440 --> 00:12.160
This date could represent an event like a birth date.

00:12.440 --> 00:13.200
Happy birthday.

00:15.960 --> 00:16.760
Happy birthday.

00:18.160 --> 00:20.320
Or a project deadline at your work.

00:20.360 --> 00:22.440
And mainly it has three components.

00:22.440 --> 00:26.160
The first part is a four digit number indicating the year.

00:26.200 --> 00:28.760
Then the next component it is the month.

00:28.760 --> 00:33.160
So normally we represent the month with a number between 1 and 12.

00:33.160 --> 00:35.320
And the last component is the day.

00:35.360 --> 00:38.520
This is a number between 1 and 31 depending on the month.

00:38.560 --> 00:42.920
Now in database we call this structure of the three components a date.

00:42.920 --> 00:45.560
So this is what we mean with dates in SQL.

00:45.600 --> 00:45.920
All right.

00:45.920 --> 00:47.240
So now let's move to the next one.

00:47.240 --> 00:48.160
What is time.

00:48.200 --> 00:51.280
Time refers to a specific point within a day.

00:51.280 --> 00:56.320
Like for example we have 18:00 55 minutes and 45 seconds.

00:56.320 --> 00:59.120
So this structure has as well three components.

00:59.160 --> 01:01.040
The first one we call it the hours.

01:01.080 --> 01:06.120
It is as well a number between 0 and 23 indicating the hour of the day.

01:06.160 --> 01:08.040
Then the next one it is the minutes.

01:08.040 --> 01:10.360
This is a number between 0 and 59.

01:10.400 --> 01:12.680
Moving on to the last component, we have the second.

01:12.720 --> 01:17.280
This is again the same thing in number between 0 and 59.

01:17.280 --> 01:22.160
So now this structure with all three components we call it in databases and SQL a time.

01:22.160 --> 01:24.040
So this is what we mean with the time.

01:24.320 --> 01:25.520
Now to the last type.

01:25.520 --> 01:31.640
If you go and combine both the date together with the time and you put them side by side, you will

01:31.640 --> 01:37.160
get a new structure and a new name in the databases and we call it usually timestamp.

01:37.160 --> 01:42.840
This name is used in many databases like Oracle, Postgres and MySQL, but in the SQL server we have

01:42.840 --> 01:43.760
another name for that.

01:43.760 --> 01:45.480
We call it date time.

01:45.480 --> 01:46.600
So again it's very simple.

01:46.600 --> 01:51.640
The date time or timestamp has the date information together with the time information.

01:51.640 --> 01:54.720
So here in this example we have six components from left to right.

01:54.720 --> 01:57.200
And here we have like a hierarchy in this structure.

01:57.200 --> 01:59.840
So we start with the highest which is the year.

01:59.880 --> 02:02.080
Then we have the month the day.

02:02.120 --> 02:05.520
And then we continue to the hour minutes and seconds.

02:05.520 --> 02:09.160
So those are the three different types about date and time information.

02:09.160 --> 02:15.360
In SQL we have the date alone or the time alone or together in the date time.

02:15.360 --> 02:15.680
All right.

02:15.680 --> 02:21.120
Let's explore now the data that we have inside our database searching for date and time informations.

02:21.160 --> 02:23.160
Now let's go to the table orders.

02:23.160 --> 02:27.640
And if you go and expand it you will find here two columns having the data type date.

02:27.640 --> 02:32.480
So we have the order dates with the date and as well the shipping date with the data type dates.

02:32.480 --> 02:35.200
And if you check the last column the creation date.

02:35.200 --> 02:37.240
This one is date time two.

02:37.320 --> 02:40.720
So now let's go and query those informations in order to understand the structure.

02:40.840 --> 02:51.880
I'm just going to select the order ID, the order date and the ship date and the creation time from

02:52.200 --> 02:54.880
sales orders and from his big.

02:54.880 --> 02:56.240
So let's go and execute it.

02:56.240 --> 03:01.600
Now if we go and check both order date and ship date you can find that here we have only the structure

03:01.600 --> 03:05.440
or the informations about the dates and we have nothing about the time.

03:05.440 --> 03:10.000
So again here we have a year, month and day and that's why they have the data type date.

03:10.040 --> 03:12.040
Now let's go and check the creation time.

03:12.080 --> 03:16.200
Not only we have the date information but as well we have the time information.

03:16.200 --> 03:18.920
So it starts with the date information year month day.

03:19.040 --> 03:22.200
And then we have our minute and seconds.

03:22.200 --> 03:25.360
And then we have fractions of the seconds milliseconds and so on.

03:25.360 --> 03:28.920
So this is how the date time or timestamp looks like in databases.

03:29.160 --> 03:31.400
And this is how the date looks like.
